(function(E){ const x = E["exam-07"] = E["exam-07"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x07-r3"] = {"id":"x07-r3","patterns":["RA-tech","GT3-life","PARA-research"],"title":{"en":"Reading 3: Passage 3 / Section 3","tr":"Reading 3: Passage 3 / Section 3","fa":"Reading ۳: متن ۳ (Passage 3) / بخش ۳ (Section 3)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to match statements to the expert who made them, complete sentences with the right ending, and answer multiple-choice questions on a passage that compares several views.","tr":"Bu derste ifadeleri onları söyleyen uzmanla eşleştirmeyi, cümleleri doğru sonla tamamlamayı ve birkaç görüşü karşılaştıran bir metin üzerine çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جمله‌ها را به کارشناسی که گفته وصل کنی، جمله‌ها را با پایان درست کامل کنی و به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای درباره‌ی متنی که چند نظر را مقایسه می‌کند جواب بدهی."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to find which of nine paragraphs contains each piece of information, and to match statements to the five people quoted in a long article.","tr":"Bu derste her bilginin dokuz paragraftan hangisinde olduğunu bulmayı ve ifadeleri uzun bir yazıda alıntı yapılan beş kişiyle eşleştirmeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری پیدا کنی هر اطلاعات در کدام یک از نُه پاراگراف است و جمله‌ها را با پنج نفری که در یک مقاله‌ی بلند از آن‌ها نقل‌قول شده جور کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 3: experts compared","tr":"Reading Passage 3: uzmanlar karşılaştırılıyor","fa":"Reading Passage 3: مقایسه‌ی کارشناس‌ها"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to match statements to the expert who made them, complete sentences with the right ending, and answer multiple-choice questions on a passage that compares several views.","tr":"Bu derste ifadeleri onları söyleyen uzmanla eşleştirmeyi, cümleleri doğru sonla tamamlamayı ve birkaç görüşü karşılaştıran bir metin üzerine çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جمله‌ها را به کارشناسی که گفته وصل کنی، جمله‌ها را با پایان درست کامل کنی و به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای درباره‌ی متنی که چند نظر را مقایسه می‌کند جواب بدهی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"14"},{"label":{"en":"Experts","tr":"Uzman","fa":"کارشناس"},"value":"3"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: delivery robots","tr":"Bu sınav: teslimat robotları","fa":"این آزمون: ربات‌های تحویل"},"intro":{"en":"Technology, cities and business are a regular Passage 3 subject. Passages that compare several experts test whether you can keep track of who thinks what, even when each person appears more than once.","tr":"Teknoloji, şehirler ve iş düzenli bir Passage 3 konusudur. Birkaç uzmanı karşılaştıran metinler, her kişi birden fazla kez görünse bile kimin ne düşündüğünü takip edip edemediğini ölçer.","fa":"فناوری، شهر و کسب‌وکار موضوع همیشگی Passage 3 است. متن‌هایی که چند کارشناس را مقایسه می‌کنند می‌سنجند که می‌توانی دنبال کنی چه کسی چه فکری دارد یا نه، حتی وقتی هر نفر بیش از یک بار می‌آید."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x07-r3-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-tech","PARA-research"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-tech","n":18,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Three experts on a new technology","tr":"Yeni bir teknoloji üzerine üç uzman","fa":"سه کارشناس درباره‌ی یک فناوری تازه"},"asks":{"en":"A passage brings together three experts who look at the same new technology from different angles: an engineer, a planner and an economist. You match each statement to the expert who makes it.","tr":"Bir metin aynı yeni teknolojiye farklı açılardan bakan üç uzmanı bir araya getiriyor: bir mühendis, bir şehir plancısı ve bir ekonomist. Her ifadeyi onu söyleyen uzmanla eşleştirirsin.","fa":"متنی سه کارشناس را کنار هم می‌آورد که از زاویه‌های مختلف به یک فناوری تازه نگاه می‌کنند: یک مهندس، یک برنامه‌ریز شهری و یک اقتصاددان. هر جمله را به کارشناسی که آن را می‌گوید وصل می‌کنی."},"fields":["The engineer’s view","The planner’s view","The economist’s view","Limits of the technology","Costs and jobs","What they agree on"],"words":[{"a":"the main obstacle","b":"the biggest problem / what still holds it back","tr":"asıl engel","fa":"مانع اصلی"},{"a":"struggle with","b":"find it hard to deal with","tr":"... ile zorlanmak","fa":"با ... مشکل داشتن"},{"a":"frank","b":"honest / open","tr":"açık sözlü","fa":"رک"},{"a":"cope badly with","b":"do not work well in","tr":"... ile iyi başa çıkamamak","fa":"از پسِ ... خوب برنیامدن"},{"a":"from the point of view of","b":"looking at it as","tr":"... açısından","fa":"از دیدِ"},{"a":"does not oppose","b":"is not against","tr":"karşı değil","fa":"مخالف نیست"},{"a":"consulted","b":"asked for their opinion","tr":"danışılmış","fa":"نظرخواهی‌شده"},{"a":"currently","b":"at the moment / for now","tr":"şu anda","fa":"در حال حاضر"},{"a":"cautious","b":"careful / not sure","tr":"temkinli","fa":"محتاط"},{"a":"unclear","b":"nobody really knows yet","tr":"belirsiz","fa":"نامعلوم"},{"a":"all three agree","b":"on one point they share a view","tr":"üçü de hemfikir","fa":"هر سه موافق‌اند"},{"a":"in the near future","b":"soon / in the next few years","tr":"yakın gelecekte","fa":"در آینده‌ی نزدیک"}],"traps":[{"en":"Whose view? An expert may describe what supporters or critics claim before giving a different opinion. Match the statement to the person who actually holds it.","tr":"Kimin görüşü? Bir uzman farklı bir görüş vermeden önce destekçilerin ya da eleştirmenlerin ne iddia ettiğini anlatabilir. İfadeyi onu gerçekten savunan kişiyle eşleştir.","fa":"نظرِ کیست؟ ممکن است کارشناسی قبل از گفتن نظر متفاوتش، ادعای طرفدارها یا منتقدها را بگوید. جمله را به کسی وصل کن که واقعاً همان نظر را دارد."},{"en":"An expert can appear in more than one paragraph. Read all of each person’s comments before you decide.","tr":"Bir uzman birden fazla paragrafta görünebilir. Karar vermeden önce her kişinin bütün yorumlarını oku.","fa":"ممکن است یک کارشناس در بیش از یک پاراگراف بیاید. قبل از تصمیم، همه‌ی حرف‌های هر نفر را بخوان."},{"en":"A sentence ending can be true in general but not stated in the passage, like a prediction no expert makes.","tr":"Bir cümle sonu genel olarak doğru olabilir ama metinde söylenmemiş olabilir; hiçbir uzmanın yapmadığı bir tahmin gibi.","fa":"ممکن است پایان جمله‌ای به‌طور کلی درست باشد اما در متن نیامده باشد، مثل پیش‌بینی‌ای که هیچ کارشناسی نمی‌کند."}],"example":{"text":"\"Critics say the new trains are too expensive. The engineer Tom Ashe disagrees: ‘Over thirty years, they will cost less to run than the old ones.’\"","item":"Statement: The trains will save money in the long run. Who says this?","answer":"Tom Ashe","why":{"en":"The critics say \"too expensive\"; Ashe says they \"will cost less to run\" over thirty years.","tr":"Eleştirmenler \"çok pahalı\" diyor; Ashe otuz yılda \"işletmesinin daha ucuz olacağını\" söylüyor.","fa":"منتقدها می‌گویند «خیلی گران است»؛ اَش می‌گوید در سی سال «هزینه‌ی کارکردشان کمتر می‌شود»."}}},{"id":"RA-tech-research","ctx":["RA-tech"],"title":{"en":"Technology, business and cities: experts compared","tr":"Teknoloji, iş dünyası ve şehirler: uzman görüşleri","fa":"فناوری، کسب‌وکار و شهرها: مقایسه‌ی نظر متخصص‌ها"},"asks":{"en":"A report on technology, business or cities that compares experts’ views: driverless cars, robot referees, green roofs, company boards. Matching features links each view to an expert; multiple choice tests why the writer gives an example.","tr":"Teknoloji, iş dünyası ya da şehirler üzerine uzman görüşlerini karşılaştıran bir rapor: sürücüsüz arabalar, robot hakemler, yeşil çatılar, şirket yönetim kurulları. Özellik eşleştirme her görüşü bir uzmana bağlar; çoktan seçmeli sorular yazarın bir örneği neden verdiğini sınar.","fa":"گزارشی درباره‌ی فناوری، کسب‌وکار یا شهرها که نظر متخصص‌ها را مقایسه می‌کند: خودروی بی‌راننده، داور رباتیک، بام سبز، هیئت‌مدیره‌ی شرکت‌ها. جورکردن ویژگی‌ها هر نظر را به یک متخصص وصل می‌کند؛ سؤال چندگزینه‌ای می‌پرسد نویسنده چرا مثالی را آورده."},"fields":["Which expert warns about the cost?","Which company was the first to try it?","The writer mentions the stadium in order to...","Green roofs are most useful when... (sentence ending)"],"words":[{"a":"benefit","b":"advantage / gain","tr":"yarar","fa":"سود"},{"a":"drawback","b":"disadvantage / downside","tr":"dezavantaj","fa":"عیب"},{"a":"reduce","b":"cut / bring down","tr":"azaltmak","fa":"کاهش دادن"},{"a":"investment","b":"money spent at the start","tr":"yatırım","fa":"سرمایه‌گذاری"},{"a":"adopt","b":"start using / take up","tr":"benimsemek","fa":"به کار گرفتن"},{"a":"reliable","b":"can be trusted / works every time","tr":"güvenilir","fa":"قابل اعتماد"},{"a":"regulation","b":"rules / the law","tr":"düzenleme","fa":"مقررات"},{"a":"consumers","b":"customers / the public","tr":"tüketiciler","fa":"مصرف‌کننده‌ها"},{"a":"predicts","b":"expects / forecasts","tr":"öngörür","fa":"پیش‌بینی می‌کند"},{"a":"warns","b":"points out the risk","tr":"uyarır","fa":"هشدار می‌دهد"},{"a":"widespread","b":"common / in many places","tr":"yaygın","fa":"گسترده"},{"a":"enthusiastic","b":"very positive about it","tr":"hevesli","fa":"مشتاق"}],"traps":[{"en":"Two experts mention cost; only one says it is the main problem. Match the whole statement.","tr":"İki uzman maliyetten söz eder; yalnızca biri asıl sorunun bu olduğunu söyler. İfadenin tamamını eşleştir.","fa":"دو متخصص از هزینه حرف می‌زنند؛ فقط یکی می‌گوید مشکل اصلی همین است. کل جمله را جور کن."},{"en":"Writer’s purpose: the answer is why the example is there, not what the example says.","tr":"Yazarın amacı: cevap örneğin ne söylediği değil, neden orada olduğudur.","fa":"هدف نویسنده: جواب این است که چرا مثال آنجاست، نه اینکه مثال چه می‌گوید."}],"example":{"text":"The engineer Maria Costa believes driverless buses will be common within ten years. The economist Paul Hart is less sure: the technology may be ready, he says, but the law is not.","item":"Who thinks that rules and laws will slow progress?  A Maria Costa   B Paul Hart","answer":"B","why":{"en":"\"The law is not [ready]\" = regulation will slow it down. That is Hart’s view.","tr":"\"Yasa hazır değil\" = düzenlemeler ilerlemeyi yavaşlatacak. Bu Hart’ın görüşü.","fa":"«قانون آماده نیست» = مقررات پیشرفت را کند می‌کند. این نظر هارت است."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-tech"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-tech","n":18,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"People, endings, then four options","tr":"Kişiler, sonlar, sonra dört seçenek","fa":"آدم‌ها، پایان‌ها، بعد چهار گزینه"},"body":{"en":"Questions 27-33: match each statement to one of three experts, A-C; letters can be used more than once. Questions 34-36: choose the correct ending for each sentence from five, A-E. Questions 37-40: choose A, B, C or D.","tr":"Soru 27-33: her ifadeyi A-C arası üç uzmandan biriyle eşleştir; harfler birden fazla kullanılabilir. Soru 34-36: her cümle için beş sondan A-E doğru olanı seç. Soru 37-40: A, B, C ya da D’yi seç.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۲۷ تا ۳۳: هر جمله را به یکی از سه کارشناس، A تا C، وصل کن؛ حرف‌ها می‌توانند بیش از یک بار بیایند. سؤال‌های ۳۴ تا ۳۶: برای هر جمله از پنج پایان، A تا E، پایان درست را انتخاب کن. سؤال‌های ۳۷ تا ۴۰: A، B، C یا D را انتخاب کن."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"A map of who says what","tr":"Kim ne diyor haritası","fa":"نقشه‌ی اینکه چه کسی چه می‌گوید"},"steps":[{"en":"Circle each expert’s name every time it appears, and note one word for their main concern.","tr":"Her uzmanın adını her geçtiği yerde daire içine al ve ana kaygısı için bir kelime not et.","fa":"هر بار اسم یک کارشناس می‌آید دورش خط بکش و برای دغدغه‌ی اصلی‌اش یک کلمه یادداشت کن."},{"en":"For each statement, find the idea in the passage and check whose words they are.","tr":"Her ifade için fikri metinde bul ve sözlerin kime ait olduğuna bak.","fa":"برای هر جمله، ایده را در متن پیدا کن و ببین حرفِ چه کسی است."},{"en":"For sentence endings, check grammar first, then meaning; two endings will not be used.","tr":"Cümle sonlarında önce dil bilgisine, sonra anlama bak; iki son kullanılmayacak.","fa":"برای پایان جمله‌ها اول دستور را بسنج، بعد معنی را؛ دو پایان استفاده نمی‌شوند."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Reported claims","tr":"Aktarılan iddialar","fa":"ادعاهای نقل‌شده"},"body":{"en":"Experts often begin by describing what other people say: supporters promise, critics warn. Their own view comes afterwards, often after \"but\", \"however\" or \"argues\". Match the statement only to someone who holds it, not to someone who reports it.","tr":"Uzmanlar çoğu zaman başkalarının söylediklerini anlatarak başlar: destekçiler vaat eder, eleştirmenler uyarır. Kendi görüşleri sonra, çoğu zaman \"but\", \"however\" ya da \"argues\"tan sonra gelir. İfadeyi yalnızca onu savunan biriyle eşleştir, aktaranla değil.","fa":"کارشناس‌ها اغلب با گفتنِ حرف دیگران شروع می‌کنند: طرفدارها قول می‌دهند، منتقدها هشدار می‌دهند. نظر خودشان بعد می‌آید، اغلب بعد از «but»، «however» یا «argues». جمله را فقط به کسی وصل کن که آن نظر را دارد، نه به کسی که نقلش می‌کند."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"Matching an expert, step by step","tr":"Bir uzmanı eşleştirmek, adım adım","fa":"وصل کردن یک کارشناس، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Match the statement with the correct expert.","text":"\"The doctor Eva Lind accepts that the app is popular. ‘But popularity is not proof,’ she says. ‘We need a proper trial.’ The designer Ben Hale is more confident: ‘Users tell us it works.’\"","item":"Statement: More evidence is needed before the app can be trusted. A Eva Lind  B Ben Hale","answer":"A","walk":[{"en":"Find both names and their words.","tr":"İki ismi ve sözlerini bul.","fa":"هر دو اسم و حرف‌هایشان را پیدا کن."},{"en":"Lind: \"popularity is not proof... we need a proper trial\" = more evidence needed.","tr":"Lind: \"popülerlik kanıt değildir... düzgün bir deneye ihtiyacımız var\" = daha fazla kanıt gerekli.","fa":"لیند: «محبوبیت دلیل نیست... به یک آزمایش درست نیاز داریم» یعنی شواهد بیشتری لازم است."},{"en":"Hale relies on what users say: the opposite view. Answer: A.","tr":"Hale kullanıcıların söylediklerine güveniyor: zıt görüş. Cevap: A.","fa":"هِیل به حرف کاربرها تکیه می‌کند: نظری مخالف. جواب: A."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"\"Supporters say the bridge will end traffic jams. The planner Rosa Kemp is doubtful: ‘It will help for a year or two, then the traffic will grow again.’\" What does Kemp think?","options":["The bridge will end traffic jams.","The bridge will not solve the problem for long.","The bridge should not be built."],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The supporters make the promise; Kemp expects only a short-term improvement. She does not say it should not be built.","tr":"Vaadi destekçiler veriyor; Kemp yalnızca kısa süreli bir iyileşme bekliyor. İnşa edilmemesi gerektiğini söylemiyor.","fa":"قول را طرفدارها می‌دهند؛ کمپ فقط بهبودی کوتاه‌مدت انتظار دارد. نمی‌گوید نباید ساخته شود."}},"remember":{"en":"Track every expert through the passage, separate their view from the views they report, and check grammar before meaning for endings.","tr":"Her uzmanı metin boyunca izle, görüşlerini aktardıkları görüşlerden ayır ve cümle sonlarında anlamdan önce dil bilgisine bak.","fa":"هر کارشناس را در طول متن دنبال کن، نظر خودش را از نظرهایی که نقل می‌کند جدا کن و برای پایان جمله‌ها قبل از معنی دستور را بسنج."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x07-r3-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-07","unit":"x07-r3"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 3","title":{"en":"Robots on the pavement","tr":"Kaldırımdaki robotlar","fa":"ربات‌ها در پیاده‌رو"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-tech"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.","passage":"Robots on the pavement\n\nIn a growing number of suburbs and university campuses, a strange sight has become ordinary: a small, six-wheeled box rolling along the pavement at walking pace, stopping politely at kerbs and waiting for a gap in the traffic before crossing. Inside is someone's shopping or takeaway dinner. Supporters of these delivery robots say they will make deliveries cheaper, cleaner and faster. Critics warn that they will crowd the pavements and put couriers out of work. Three experts who have studied the robots closely suggest that the truth is more complicated than either side admits.\n\nFor Samuel Achterberg, a robotics engineer who has tested several models, the technology itself is no longer the main obstacle. \"On a quiet, simple route, a modern delivery robot can find its way perfectly well,\" he says. \"Mapping and navigation are largely solved problems.\" What the robots still struggle with, he argues, is people. Dogs bark at them, children sit on them, and adults occasionally kick them or block their way to see what will happen. When a robot cannot decide what to do, it stops and calls for help from a remote operator, who watches through its cameras and guides it past the problem. One operator can supervise several robots at once, but the need for human help shows how far the machines still are from working entirely on their own.\n\nAchterberg is also frank about the robots' physical limits. Their batteries last for a few hours at most, and they cope badly with heavy snow, which hides the edges of pavements and kerbs. Most importantly, they are slow. \"They move at the speed of a person walking,\" he says, \"so they only make sense over short distances, typically a couple of kilometres at most. Nobody is going to wait two hours for a robot to cross a city.\"\n\nDana Whitcombe, an urban planner, approaches the question from the point of view of the street. Pavements, she points out, were designed for people, and they are already crowded in many places. A handful of robots causes no difficulty, but hundreds could make pavements harder to use for those who already find them difficult, such as wheelchair users and parents with pushchairs. Yet Whitcombe does not oppose the technology. If robots replaced some of the vans that now stop on busy roads to drop off parcels, she believes, the result could be less traffic and cleaner air. In her view, the real question is not whether robots belong on the street, but how many, and on which streets.\n\nCities have responded in very different ways. Some have welcomed the robots as a sign of innovation, while a few have banned them from their pavements altogether. Whitcombe's view is that neither approach is wise. She argues that robots should be introduced through limited trials, and that residents should be consulted before they arrive, rather than finding them on their doorstep one morning. Trials of this kind, she says, also give planners the evidence they need to decide where the robots cause problems and where they do not.\n\nThe economist Rafael Montes is interested in a different question: do the robots actually save money? The final stage of a delivery, from the local warehouse to the customer's door, is known as the \"last mile\", and it is usually the most expensive part of the whole journey. Robots appear to offer a cheaper way of covering it. However, Montes points out that once the cost of remote operators, repairs and charging is included, each delivery currently costs more than it would with a human courier. He expects this to change as the robots improve and are built in larger numbers, but not quickly.\n\nMontes is also cautious about the effect on jobs. Some courier work may disappear, but the robots create new work too, for remote operators, mechanics and the staff who load them. \"The overall effect on employment is genuinely unclear,\" he says. He adds that customers may not be as eager for speed as companies assume. In surveys, many say they would prefer to pay less and wait a little longer, rather than pay extra for a delivery within the hour.\n\nOn one point, all three experts agree. Small delivery robots are unlikely to replace delivery vans in the near future. They are suited to light goods, short distances and quiet streets, and that leaves a great deal of work for which they are simply not designed. Where the experts differ is in how much they expect this to change, and how quickly.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 27-33. Look at the following statements (Questions 27-33) and the list of experts below. Match each statement with the correct expert, A, B or C. Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 27-33 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-features","bank":["A Samuel Achterberg","B Dana Whitcombe","C Rafael Montes"],"questions":[{"n":27,"kind":"match","prompt":"The hardest problem for the robots is the behaviour of people.","correct":0,"evidence":"What the robots still struggle with, he argues, is people","why":{"en":"Achterberg: navigation is \"largely solved\"; \"what the robots still struggle with... is people\".","tr":"Achterberg: yön bulma \"büyük ölçüde çözüldü\"; \"robotların hâlâ zorlandığı şey... insanlar\".","fa":"آختربرگ: مسیریابی «تا حد زیادی حل شده»؛ «چیزی که ربات‌ها هنوز با آن مشکل دارند... آدم‌ها هستند»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":28,"kind":"match","prompt":"Large numbers of robots could make pavements harder for some people to use.","correct":1,"evidence":"hundreds could make pavements harder to use","why":{"en":"Whitcombe: hundreds of robots \"could make pavements harder to use\" for wheelchair users and parents with pushchairs.","tr":"Whitcombe: yüzlerce robot tekerlekli sandalye kullananlar ve bebek arabalı ebeveynler için \"kaldırımları kullanmayı zorlaştırabilir\".","fa":"وایتکام: صدها ربات «می‌توانند استفاده از پیاده‌رو را سخت‌تر کنند» برای کسانی که ویلچر یا کالسکه دارند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":29,"kind":"match","prompt":"At present, a robot delivery costs more than one made by a person.","correct":2,"evidence":"each delivery currently costs more than it would with a human courier","why":{"en":"Montes: once all costs are included, \"each delivery currently costs more than it would with a human courier\".","tr":"Montes: tüm maliyetler eklendiğinde \"her teslimat şu anda bir kuryeyle olacağından daha pahalı\".","fa":"مونتس: وقتی همه‌ی هزینه‌ها حساب شود، «هر تحویل در حال حاضر گران‌تر از تحویل با پیک انسانی است»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":30,"kind":"match","prompt":"The robots are only useful over short distances.","correct":0,"evidence":"they only make sense over short distances","why":{"en":"Achterberg: they move at walking speed, \"so they only make sense over short distances\".","tr":"Achterberg: yürüme hızında ilerliyorlar, \"bu yüzden yalnızca kısa mesafelerde anlamlılar\".","fa":"آختربرگ: با سرعت راه رفتن حرکت می‌کنند، «پس فقط برای فاصله‌های کوتاه معنی دارند»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]},{"n":31,"kind":"match","prompt":"The robots may create jobs as well as remove them.","correct":2,"evidence":"the robots create new work too","why":{"en":"Montes: some courier work may disappear, \"but the robots create new work too\".","tr":"Montes: bazı kurye işleri kaybolabilir \"ama robotlar yeni işler de yaratıyor\".","fa":"مونتس: شاید بخشی از کار پیک‌ها از بین برود، «اما ربات‌ها کار تازه هم می‌سازند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":32,"kind":"match","prompt":"Local people should be asked for their views before robots are introduced.","correct":1,"evidence":"residents should be consulted before they arrive","why":{"en":"Whitcombe: robots should come through trials, and \"residents should be consulted before they arrive\".","tr":"Whitcombe: robotlar denemelerle gelmeli ve \"gelmeden önce bölge sakinlerine danışılmalı\".","fa":"وایتکام: ربات‌ها باید با آزمایش بیایند و «قبل از آمدنشان باید با ساکنان مشورت شود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":33,"kind":"match","prompt":"The robots could lead to fewer delivery vans on the roads.","correct":1,"evidence":"If robots replaced some of the vans","why":{"en":"Whitcombe: \"If robots replaced some of the vans... the result could be less traffic and cleaner air.\"","tr":"Whitcombe: \"Robotlar kamyonetlerin bir kısmının yerini alırsa... sonuç daha az trafik ve daha temiz hava olabilir.\"","fa":"وایتکام: «اگر ربات‌ها جای بعضی از ون‌ها را بگیرند... نتیجه می‌تواند ترافیک کمتر و هوای پاک‌تر باشد»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 34-36. Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-E, below. Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 34-36 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"sentence-endings","bank":["A have stopped the robots from using their pavements.","B are needed when a robot cannot solve a problem itself.","C will be replaced by drones within ten years.","D is normally the costliest stage of the journey.","E make most of their deliveries at night."],"questions":[{"n":34,"kind":"match","prompt":"Remote operators","correct":1,"evidence":"it stops and calls for help from a remote operator","why":{"en":"When a robot cannot decide what to do, \"it stops and calls for help from a remote operator\": B.","tr":"Robot ne yapacağına karar veremeyince \"durup uzaktaki bir operatörden yardım istiyor\": B.","fa":"وقتی ربات نمی‌تواند تصمیم بگیرد، «می‌ایستد و از یک اپراتور از راه دور کمک می‌خواهد»: B."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":35,"kind":"match","prompt":"The \"last mile\" of a delivery","correct":3,"evidence":"it is usually the most expensive part of the whole journey","why":{"en":"\"It is usually the most expensive part of the whole journey\": D.","tr":"\"Genelde tüm yolculuğun en pahalı kısmıdır\": D.","fa":"«معمولاً گران‌ترین بخش کل مسیر است»: D."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":36,"kind":"match","prompt":"Some cities","correct":0,"evidence":"a few have banned them from their pavements altogether","why":{"en":"\"A few have banned them from their pavements altogether\": A. Drones (C) are not mentioned.","tr":"\"Birkaçı onları kaldırımlarından tamamen yasakladı\": A. Dronlardan (C) söz edilmiyor.","fa":"«چندتایی آن‌ها را کلاً از پیاده‌روهایشان ممنوع کرده‌اند»: A. از پهپاد (C) حرفی نیست."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 37-40. Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"mcq","questions":[{"n":37,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What is the writer’s purpose in the first paragraph?","options":["A to introduce opposing views about the robots","B to describe how the robots were invented","C to argue that the robots should be banned","D to explain how the robots find their way"],"correct":0,"evidence":"Three experts who have studied the robots closely suggest that the truth is more complicated","why":{"en":"The paragraph sets out what supporters say and what critics warn, then introduces the experts. It argues for neither side.","tr":"Paragraf destekçilerin ne dediğini ve eleştirmenlerin neyi uyardığını ortaya koyuyor, sonra uzmanları tanıtıyor. Hiçbir tarafı savunmuyor.","fa":"پاراگراف حرف طرفدارها و هشدار منتقدها را می‌گوید و بعد کارشناس‌ها را معرفی می‌کند. از هیچ طرفی دفاع نمی‌کند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":38,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"According to Achterberg, the robots work badly","options":["A on busy main roads.","B in heavy snow.","C at night.","D on steep hills."],"correct":1,"evidence":"they cope badly with heavy snow","why":{"en":"\"They cope badly with heavy snow, which hides the edges of pavements and kerbs.\"","tr":"\"Yoğun karla iyi baş edemiyorlar; kar kaldırımların ve bordürlerin kenarlarını gizliyor.\"","fa":"«در برف سنگین بد کار می‌کنند، چون برف لبه‌ی پیاده‌رو و جدول را می‌پوشاند»."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":39,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What does Montes say about customers?","options":["A Most want deliveries within the hour.","B They prefer robots to human couriers.","C Many accept slower delivery if it costs less.","D They are worried about the safety of robots."],"correct":2,"evidence":"they would prefer to pay less and wait a little longer","why":{"en":"In surveys, many customers \"would prefer to pay less and wait a little longer\". A is what companies assume.","tr":"Anketlerde birçok müşteri \"daha az ödeyip biraz daha uzun beklemeyi tercih ediyor\". A şirketlerin varsaydığı şey.","fa":"در نظرسنجی‌ها خیلی از مشتری‌ها «ترجیح می‌دهند کمتر بپردازند و کمی بیشتر صبر کنند». A چیزی است که شرکت‌ها فرض می‌کنند."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-samewords"]},{"n":40,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What do all three experts agree about?","options":["A The robots will soon be cheaper than couriers.","B Cities should ban the robots.","C The technology is not yet safe.","D Vans will still be needed for some time yet."],"correct":3,"evidence":"Small delivery robots are unlikely to replace delivery vans in the near future","why":{"en":"\"On one point, all three experts agree\": the robots \"are unlikely to replace delivery vans in the near future\".","tr":"\"Bir noktada üç uzman da hemfikir\": robotların \"yakın gelecekte teslimat kamyonetlerinin yerini alması olası değil\".","fa":"«در یک نکته هر سه کارشناس موافق‌اند»: ربات‌ها «احتمالاً در آینده‌ی نزدیک جای ون‌های تحویل را نمی‌گیرند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]}],"id":"c-x07-r3-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-07","unit":"x07-r3"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The engineer is frank about the robots’ limits.\" Frank means...","options":["honest and direct","worried","proud"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Frank = saying openly what you think.","tr":"Frank = düşündüğünü açıkça söyleyen.","fa":"frank یعنی رک و صریح."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":2,"prompt":"A statement says \"Residents should be asked first.\" Which words in a passage mean the same?","options":["residents complained afterwards","residents were not informed","local people should be consulted beforehand"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Consulted beforehand = asked first.","tr":"Önceden danışılmak = önce sorulmak.","fa":"consulted beforehand یعنی اول از آن‌ها پرسیده شود."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"An expert’s name appears in paragraphs 2 and 3. A statement seems to match paragraph 3 but uses different words. What do you do?","options":["Match only the words in paragraph 2","Check the meaning in paragraph 3 before matching","Skip the statement"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Match the meaning, and read every place the expert appears.","tr":"Anlamı eşleştir ve uzmanın göründüğü her yeri oku.","fa":"معنی را جور کن و همه‌ی جاهایی را که کارشناس می‌آید بخوان."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"\"Supporters claim the robots will cut traffic. The planner, however, believes the effect will be small.\" Whose view is \"The robots will greatly reduce traffic\"?","options":["the supporters","the planner","both"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The planner reports the claim and then disagrees.","tr":"Plancı iddiayı aktarıp sonra karşı çıkıyor.","fa":"برنامه‌ریز ادعا را نقل می‌کند و بعد مخالفت می‌کند."}}],"id":"c-x07-r3-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-07","unit":"x07-r3"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 3: paragraphs and people","tr":"GT Reading Section 3: paragraflar ve kişiler","fa":"GT Reading Section 3: پاراگراف‌ها و آدم‌ها"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to find which of nine paragraphs contains each piece of information, and to match statements to the five people quoted in a long article.","tr":"Bu derste her bilginin dokuz paragraftan hangisinde olduğunu bulmayı ve ifadeleri uzun bir yazıda alıntı yapılan beş kişiyle eşleştirmeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری پیدا کنی هر اطلاعات در کدام یک از نُه پاراگراف است و جمله‌ها را با پنج نفری که در یک مقاله‌ی بلند از آن‌ها نقل‌قول شده جور کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Paragraphs","tr":"Paragraf","fa":"پاراگراف"},"value":"A-I"},{"label":{"en":"People","tr":"Kişi","fa":"آدم‌ها"},"value":"A-E"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: solar panels on city roofs","tr":"Bu sınav: şehir çatılarında güneş panelleri","fa":"این آزمون: پنل‌های خورشیدی روی بام‌های شهر"},"intro":{"en":"GT Section 3 is one long article. Society, work and everyday life are common subjects, and articles about a local project often quote several people with different roles.","tr":"GT Section 3 tek bir uzun yazıdır. Toplum, iş ve günlük yaşam sık konulardır ve yerel bir proje hakkındaki yazılar çoğu zaman farklı rollerdeki birkaç kişiden alıntı yapar.","fa":"GT Section 3 یک مقاله‌ی بلند است. جامعه، کار و زندگی روزمره موضوع‌های رایج‌اند و مقاله‌هایی درباره‌ی یک پروژه‌ی محلی اغلب از چند نفر با نقش‌های مختلف نقل‌قول می‌کنند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x07-r3gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT3-life","PARA-research"],"often":{"pattern":"GT3-life","n":14,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 14 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 14’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۴ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A city scheme and the people behind it","tr":"Bir şehir projesi ve arkasındaki insanlar","fa":"طرحی شهری و آدم‌هایی که پشتش هستند"},"asks":{"en":"A long article in nine lettered paragraphs about a change in a city. First you find which paragraph contains each piece of information; then you match five people to what they say.","tr":"Bir şehirdeki bir değişim hakkında, harflerle ayrılmış dokuz paragraflık uzun bir yazı. Önce her bilginin hangi paragrafta olduğunu bulursun; sonra beş kişiyi söyledikleriyle eşleştirirsin.","fa":"مقاله‌ای بلند در نُه پاراگرافِ حرف‌دار درباره‌ی تغییری در یک شهر. اول پیدا می‌کنی هر اطلاعات در کدام پاراگراف است و بعد پنج نفر را با حرف‌هایشان جور می‌کنی."},"fields":["The scheme","Cost","Public buildings","Flats","Old buildings","Practical problems","Storage","Jobs","The future"],"words":[{"a":"scheme","b":"a plan or programme","tr":"proje, program","fa":"طرح"},{"a":"pay for itself","b":"save as much as it cost","tr":"kendini amorti etmek","fa":"هزینه‌ی خودش را درآوردن"},{"a":"persuade","b":"get someone to agree","tr":"ikna etmek","fa":"متقاعد کردن"},{"a":"protected","b":"cannot be changed without permission","tr":"koruma altında","fa":"حفاظت‌شده"},{"a":"reluctant","b":"unwilling","tr":"isteksiz","fa":"بی‌میل"},{"a":"survey","b":"a careful inspection","tr":"inceleme, ekspertiz","fa":"بازدید فنی"},{"a":"shade","b":"shadow that blocks the sun","tr":"gölge","fa":"سایه"},{"a":"store","b":"keep for later","tr":"depolamak","fa":"ذخیره کردن"},{"a":"surplus","b":"what they do not need","tr":"fazla","fa":"مازاد"},{"a":"shortage","b":"not enough of something","tr":"eksiklik, kıtlık","fa":"کمبود"},{"a":"realistic","b":"practical / not too hopeful","tr":"gerçekçi","fa":"واقع‌بین"},{"a":"make a difference","b":"have a real effect","tr":"fark yaratmak","fa":"تأثیر واقعی گذاشتن"}],"traps":[{"en":"Which paragraph: the question uses general words (\"a problem caused by the weather\"); the paragraph uses specific ones (\"strong winds\").","tr":"Hangi paragraf: soru genel kelimeler kullanır (\"havanın yol açtığı bir sorun\"); paragraf özel kelimeler kullanır (\"güçlü rüzgârlar\").","fa":"کدام پاراگراف: سؤال کلمه‌های کلی به کار می‌برد («مشکلی که هوا ایجاد می‌کند»)؛ پاراگراف کلمه‌های مشخص («بادهای شدید»)."},{"en":"People: a person may describe a problem they solved, not a problem that still exists. Read their exact words.","tr":"Kişiler: biri artık var olan bir sorunu değil, çözdüğü bir sorunu anlatıyor olabilir. Tam sözlerini oku.","fa":"آدم‌ها: ممکن است کسی مشکلی را توصیف کند که حلش کرده، نه مشکلی که هنوز هست. حرف دقیقش را بخوان."}],"example":{"text":"\"F  ...Strong winds can lift panels that are badly fixed, so installers now use extra clips on exposed roofs.\"","item":"Which paragraph mentions a problem caused by the weather?","answer":"F","why":{"en":"\"Strong winds can lift panels\" is a weather problem, even though the question does not say \"wind\".","tr":"\"Güçlü rüzgârlar panelleri kaldırabilir\" bir hava sorunu; soru \"rüzgâr\" demese de.","fa":"«بادهای شدید می‌توانند پنل‌ها را بلند کنند» مشکلی مربوط به هواست، حتی اگر سؤال «باد» را نگوید."}}},{"id":"GT3-life","ctx":["GT3-life"],"title":{"en":"Society, work and daily life","tr":"Toplum, iş ve gündelik yaşam","fa":"جامعه، کار و زندگی روزمره"},"asks":{"en":"A text about modern life, work or society: a nursery without toys, emojis, a health programme, lessons in leadership, life in a cold town. Headings and multiple choice test the writer’s main points.","tr":"Modern yaşam, iş ya da toplum hakkında bir metin: oyuncaksız bir kreş, emojiler, bir sağlık programı, liderlik dersleri, soğuk bir kasabada yaşam. Başlıklar ve çoktan seçmeli sorular yazarın ana noktalarını sınar.","fa":"متنی درباره‌ی زندگی امروز، کار یا جامعه: مهدکودکی بدون اسباب‌بازی، ایموجی‌ها، یک برنامه‌ی سلامت، درس‌هایی درباره‌ی رهبری، زندگی در یک شهر سرد. عنوان‌ها و سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای نکته‌های اصلی نویسنده را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["An experiment that surprised parents","Mixed reactions from staff","The original purpose","Plans to expand the scheme","Which paragraph describes the results after a year?"],"words":[{"a":"scheme","b":"programme / project","tr":"program, uygulama","fa":"طرح"},{"a":"reaction","b":"response / what people thought","tr":"tepki","fa":"واکنش"},{"a":"mixed","b":"some liked it, others did not","tr":"karışık","fa":"دوگانه"},{"a":"surprising","b":"unexpected / few predicted it","tr":"şaşırtıcı","fa":"غافلگیرکننده"},{"a":"purpose","b":"aim / designed to","tr":"amaç","fa":"هدف"},{"a":"expand","b":"grow / extend to more places","tr":"genişletmek","fa":"گسترش دادن"},{"a":"residents","b":"locals / people who live there","tr":"sakinler","fa":"ساکنان"},{"a":"wellbeing","b":"health and happiness","tr":"iyi oluş","fa":"سلامت و رضایت"},{"a":"communicate","b":"express / get a message across","tr":"iletişim kurmak","fa":"ارتباط برقرار کردن"},{"a":"encourage","b":"motivate / persuade","tr":"teşvik etmek","fa":"تشویق کردن"},{"a":"trend","b":"something becoming common","tr":"eğilim","fa":"روند"},{"a":"outcome","b":"result / what happened","tr":"sonuç","fa":"نتیجه"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"Mixed reactions\" needs both sides in the paragraph. One positive comment is not enough.","tr":"\"Karışık tepkiler\" için paragrafta iki taraf da olmalı. Tek bir olumlu yorum yetmez.","fa":"«واکنش‌های دوگانه» یعنی هر دو طرف در پاراگراف باشند. یک نظر مثبت کافی نیست."},{"en":"The purpose of a scheme and its result are often in different paragraphs.","tr":"Bir uygulamanın amacı ve sonucu çoğu zaman farklı paragraflardadır.","fa":"هدف یک طرح و نتیجه‌اش اغلب در پاراگراف‌های جدا هستند."}],"example":{"text":"E  Not everyone was convinced. Several parents worried that their children would be bored without toys, while a few teachers felt the experiment had started too quickly. Others, however, praised the calmer atmosphere.","item":"Choose the heading for paragraph E:  i  Mixed reactions   ii  Children become bored   iii  How the toys were chosen","answer":"i","why":{"en":"Worries from parents and teachers, then praise from others: both sides, so mixed reactions.","tr":"Ebeveyn ve öğretmenlerin endişeleri, ardından başkalarının övgüsü: iki taraf da var, yani karışık tepkiler.","fa":"نگرانی پدر و مادرها و معلم‌ها، بعد تعریف دیگران: هر دو طرف هست، پس واکنش‌های دوگانه."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT3-life"],"often":{"pattern":"GT3-life","n":14,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 14 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 14’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۴ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Two matching tasks","tr":"İki eşleştirme görevi","fa":"دو تمرین جورکردن"},"body":{"en":"Questions 28-34: which paragraph, A-I, contains each piece of information? Some letters are not used, and a letter can be used more than once. Questions 35-40: match each statement to one of five people, A-E.","tr":"Soru 28-34: her bilgi A-I’den hangi paragrafta? Bazı harfler kullanılmaz ve bir harf birden fazla kullanılabilir. Soru 35-40: her ifadeyi A-E arası beş kişiden biriyle eşleştir.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۲۸ تا ۳۴: هر اطلاعات در کدام پاراگراف، A تا I، است؟ بعضی حرف‌ها استفاده نمی‌شوند و یک حرف ممکن است بیش از یک بار بیاید. سؤال‌های ۳۵ تا ۴۰: هر جمله را به یکی از پنج نفر، A تا E، وصل کن."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Label first, then search","tr":"Önce etiketle, sonra ara","fa":"اول برچسب بزن، بعد بگرد"},"steps":[{"en":"Skim the article once and write a two-word label next to each paragraph.","tr":"Yazıyı bir kez göz gezdir ve her paragrafın yanına iki kelimelik bir etiket yaz.","fa":"مقاله را یک بار سریع نگاه کن و کنار هر پاراگراف یک برچسب دوکلمه‌ای بنویس."},{"en":"Turn each question into a general idea (cost, animals, training) and match it to your labels, then check the paragraph.","tr":"Her soruyu genel bir fikre çevir (maliyet, hayvanlar, eğitim), etiketlerinle eşleştir, sonra paragrafı kontrol et.","fa":"هر سؤال را به یک ایده‌ی کلی تبدیل کن (هزینه، جانورها، آموزش)، با برچسب‌هایت جور کن و بعد پاراگراف را چک کن."},{"en":"For the people, circle each name and read only that person’s words.","tr":"Kişiler için her ismi daire içine al ve yalnızca o kişinin sözlerini oku.","fa":"برای آدم‌ها دور هر اسم خط بکش و فقط حرف‌های همان آدم را بخوان."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"General question, specific text","tr":"Genel soru, özel metin","fa":"سؤال کلی، متن مشخص"},"body":{"en":"The questions describe the information in general terms; the article gives specific examples. \"A problem caused by animals\" will not use the word animals. Look for the example, not the word.","tr":"Sorular bilgiyi genel ifadelerle anlatır; yazı somut örnekler verir. \"Hayvanların neden olduğu bir sorun\" ifadesi animals kelimesini kullanmayabilir. Kelimeyi değil örneği ara.","fa":"سؤال‌ها اطلاعات را با عبارت‌های کلی توصیف می‌کنند؛ مقاله مثال‌های مشخص می‌آورد. «مشکلی که جانوران ایجاد می‌کنند» ممکن است کلمه‌ی animals را نداشته باشد. دنبال مثال بگرد، نه کلمه."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"Matching a person, step by step","tr":"Bir kişiyi eşleştirmek, adım adım","fa":"وصل کردن یک نفر، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Match the statement with the correct person.","text":"\"‘We were worried about the cost,’ says Sara Holt, a shop owner, ‘but our bills have halved.’ The engineer Max Rehn adds: ‘Most problems come from poor installation.’\"","item":"Statement: Bad fitting causes most difficulties. A Sara Holt  B Max Rehn","answer":"B","walk":[{"en":"Find the idea: \"most problems come from poor installation\".","tr":"Fikri bul: \"sorunların çoğu kötü kurulumdan kaynaklanıyor\".","fa":"ایده را پیدا کن: «بیشتر مشکل‌ها از نصب بد است»."},{"en":"Check whose words they are: Max Rehn.","tr":"Sözlerin kime ait olduğuna bak: Max Rehn.","fa":"ببین حرفِ کیست: مکس رن."},{"en":"Holt talks about cost and bills, not fitting. Answer: B.","tr":"Holt kurulumdan değil, maliyet ve faturalardan söz ediyor. Cevap: B.","fa":"هولت از هزینه و قبض حرف می‌زند، نه نصب. جواب: B."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Question: \"Which paragraph mentions a lack of trained workers?\" Which sentence would you look for?","options":["\"The workers finished the job in a week.\"","\"Training sessions are held every Monday.\"","\"Firms cannot find enough qualified staff.\""],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"Cannot find enough qualified staff\" = a lack of trained workers. The others mention workers or training but not a lack.","tr":"\"Yeterli nitelikli personel bulamıyorlar\" = eğitimli işçi eksikliği. Diğerleri işçilerden ya da eğitimden söz ediyor ama eksiklikten değil.","fa":"«کارکنان واجد شرایط کافی پیدا نمی‌کنند» یعنی کمبود کارگر آموزش‌دیده. بقیه از کارگر یا آموزش حرف می‌زنند، اما نه از کمبود."}},"remember":{"en":"Label every paragraph, look for the example behind each general question, and match people by their own words.","tr":"Her paragrafı etiketle, her genel sorunun arkasındaki örneği ara ve kişileri kendi sözleriyle eşleştir.","fa":"به هر پاراگراف برچسب بزن، دنبال مثالِ پشتِ هر سؤال کلی بگرد و آدم‌ها را با حرف خودشان جور کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x07-r3-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-07","unit":"x07-r3"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 3","title":{"en":"Power from the rooftops","tr":"Çatılardan gelen enerji","fa":"برق از بام‌ها"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT3-life"],"texts":[{"title":"Power from the rooftops","kind":"article","body":"A  Seen from the top of its cathedral tower, the city of Dunmere is changing colour. Among the grey slate and red tiles, more and more roofs are now dark blue, covered with solar panels. Over the past five years, a council scheme has helped to put panels on schools, libraries, offices and blocks of flats, and the city now produces a noticeable share of its own electricity. The scheme offers free advice to building owners, helps them find approved installers and, in some cases, lends them money at a low rate of interest.\n\nB  Solar panels turn sunlight directly into electricity, and they work even on cloudy days, although they produce less. What has changed most in recent years is the price. The cost of a typical panel fell by around ninety per cent in a single decade, and the time it takes for a system to pay for itself through lower bills has fallen from more than twenty years to well under ten in many cases.\n\nC  The council began with its own buildings. \"Our first aim was simply to cut the council's energy bills,\" says Helen Brandt, who manages the scheme. \"Every pound we save on electricity is a pound we can spend on services.\" Schools were among the first to benefit. As well as saving money, many now use the panels in science lessons, with screens in the entrance hall showing pupils how much electricity the roof is producing.\n\nD  Blocks of flats have been more complicated. Joseph Mwangi, who owns a building with forty flats near the river, installed panels three years ago. \"The bills for the shared areas, the lifts and the corridor lights, have gone down by more than half,\" he says, \"and residents pay less as a result.\" The hard part, he explains, was not the technology but persuading all the owners in the building to agree to the work, which took almost two years of meetings.\n\nE  In the old centre of the city, the main problem is appearance. Many buildings are protected because of their history, and planners are reluctant to allow shiny panels on their roofs. The architect Lucia Ferraro believes this problem can be solved. \"In a historic street, what the roof looks like really matters,\" she says. Her firm uses panels designed to look like ordinary roof tiles, which are almost impossible to see from the street. They are more expensive than standard panels and produce slightly less electricity, but for many owners of old houses they are the only option the planners will accept.\n\nF  There are practical difficulties too. Owen Pritchard, an electrician who has installed panels on more than two hundred buildings, says that many roofs are not ready for them. \"Before we fit anything, we survey the roof, and on older buildings the roof often needs repairs first,\" he explains. Shade from taller buildings can also reduce the amount of electricity a system produces. And there is an unexpected problem: pigeons like to nest in the warm, sheltered space under the panels, so installers now fit wire mesh around the edges.\n\nG  A further challenge is timing. Dr Kofi Mensah, who studies energy use in cities, points out that the city needs the most electricity in the early evening, when people come home and switch on lights and cookers, just as the panels stop producing it. \"The sun and the city keep different hours,\" he says. This is why storage matters. Some buildings now have large batteries that store electricity produced during the day, and others sell what they do not need to the national grid.\n\nH  The scheme has also created work. Local firms report that they cannot find enough qualified installers, and some projects have been delayed for months as a result. To deal with the shortage, the city's college has started a one-year course in solar installation, which has more applicants than places. Students spend half their time in college and half working with local firms, and most are offered jobs before they finish.\n\nI  How far can this go? Mensah is realistic. \"A city like this will never produce all the electricity it uses from its own roofs,\" he says. \"There simply isn't enough space.\" But he believes rooftops can make a real difference, especially if panels are also fitted to the walls of tall buildings that face south. For now, Dunmere's blue roofs are a start, and other cities in the region have already sent planners to find out how the scheme works."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 28-34. The text has nine paragraphs, A-I. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-I, in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-info","bank":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"questions":[{"n":28,"kind":"match","prompt":"a problem caused by birds","correct":5,"evidence":"pigeons like to nest in the warm, sheltered space under the panels","why":{"en":"F: pigeons nest under the panels, so installers fit wire mesh.","tr":"F: güvercinler panellerin altına yuva yapıyor; bu yüzden kurulumcular tel örgü takıyor.","fa":"F: کبوترها زیر پنل‌ها لانه می‌کنند، پس نصاب‌ها توری سیمی می‌گذارند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":29,"kind":"match","prompt":"an explanation of why storing electricity is important","correct":6,"evidence":"This is why storage matters","why":{"en":"G: the city needs most electricity in the evening, when the panels stop producing it, so \"storage matters\".","tr":"G: şehir en çok elektriğe akşam, paneller üretimi bıraktığında ihtiyaç duyuyor; bu yüzden \"depolama önemli\".","fa":"G: شهر عصر، وقتی پنل‌ها دیگر برق تولید نمی‌کنند، بیشترین برق را لازم دارد؛ پس «ذخیره‌سازی مهم است»."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":30,"kind":"match","prompt":"a figure showing how much cheaper panels have become","correct":1,"evidence":"fell by around ninety per cent in a single decade","why":{"en":"B: the cost \"fell by around ninety per cent in a single decade\".","tr":"B: maliyet \"tek bir on yılda yaklaşık yüzde doksan düştü\".","fa":"B: هزینه «فقط در یک دهه حدود نود درصد کم شد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":31,"kind":"match","prompt":"a reference to the difficulty of getting people to agree","correct":3,"evidence":"persuading all the owners in the building to agree to the work","why":{"en":"D: the hard part was \"persuading all the owners in the building to agree\".","tr":"D: zor olan \"binadaki tüm sahipleri ikna etmekti\".","fa":"D: بخش سخت «راضی کردن همه‌ی مالک‌های ساختمان» بود."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":32,"kind":"match","prompt":"a way of making panels hard to notice","correct":4,"evidence":"panels designed to look like ordinary roof tiles","why":{"en":"E: panels \"designed to look like ordinary roof tiles, which are almost impossible to see from the street\".","tr":"E: \"sıradan çatı kiremitleri gibi görünecek şekilde tasarlanmış, sokaktan neredeyse görülmeyen\" paneller.","fa":"E: پنل‌هایی «طراحی‌شده شبیه سفال‌های معمولی بام که از خیابان تقریباً دیده نمی‌شوند»."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":33,"kind":"match","prompt":"a shortage of people with the right skills","correct":7,"evidence":"they cannot find enough qualified installers","why":{"en":"H: local firms \"cannot find enough qualified installers\".","tr":"H: yerel firmalar \"yeterli nitelikli kurulumcu bulamıyor\".","fa":"H: شرکت‌های محلی «نصاب واجد شرایط کافی پیدا نمی‌کنند»."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":34,"kind":"match","prompt":"a way in which panels are used to help children learn","correct":2,"evidence":"many now use the panels in science lessons","why":{"en":"C: schools \"use the panels in science lessons\". H is about training adults, not children.","tr":"C: okullar \"panelleri fen derslerinde kullanıyor\". H çocukların değil yetişkinlerin eğitimiyle ilgili.","fa":"C: مدرسه‌ها «از پنل‌ها در درس علوم استفاده می‌کنند». H درباره‌ی آموزش بزرگسال‌هاست، نه بچه‌ها."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]}]},{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 35-40. Look at the following statements (Questions 35-40) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-E. Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-features","bank":["A Helen Brandt","B Joseph Mwangi","C Lucia Ferraro","D Owen Pritchard","E Kofi Mensah"],"questions":[{"n":35,"kind":"match","prompt":"Many roofs need repairing before panels can be fitted.","correct":3,"evidence":"on older buildings the roof often needs repairs first","why":{"en":"Pritchard: \"on older buildings the roof often needs repairs first\".","tr":"Pritchard: \"eski binalarda çatının çoğu zaman önce onarılması gerekiyor\".","fa":"پریچارد: «در ساختمان‌های قدیمی‌تر اغلب اول باید بام تعمیر شود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":36,"kind":"match","prompt":"In historic areas, the appearance of a roof is important.","correct":2,"evidence":"what the roof looks like really matters","why":{"en":"Ferraro: \"In a historic street, what the roof looks like really matters.\"","tr":"Ferraro: \"Tarihî bir sokakta çatının nasıl göründüğü gerçekten önemli.\"","fa":"فرارو: «در یک خیابان تاریخی، ظاهر بام واقعاً مهم است»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":37,"kind":"match","prompt":"The scheme was started mainly to save the council money.","correct":0,"evidence":"Our first aim was simply to cut the council's energy bills","why":{"en":"Brandt: \"Our first aim was simply to cut the council’s energy bills.\"","tr":"Brandt: \"İlk amacımız sadece belediyenin enerji faturalarını azaltmaktı.\"","fa":"برانت: «هدف اولمان فقط کم کردن قبض انرژی شهرداری بود»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]},{"n":38,"kind":"match","prompt":"Electricity is needed most at the time when panels produce least.","correct":4,"evidence":"The sun and the city keep different hours","why":{"en":"Mensah: demand peaks in the early evening, \"just as the panels stop producing it\".","tr":"Mensah: talep akşamüstü zirve yapıyor, \"tam paneller üretmeyi bıraktığında\".","fa":"منسا: تقاضا اوایل عصر به اوج می‌رسد، «درست وقتی پنل‌ها تولید را متوقف می‌کنند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":39,"kind":"match","prompt":"People living in the building now spend less on bills.","correct":1,"evidence":"residents pay less as a result","why":{"en":"Mwangi: bills for the shared areas fell \"and residents pay less as a result\".","tr":"Mwangi: ortak alanların faturaları düştü \"ve sonuç olarak sakinler daha az ödüyor\".","fa":"موانگی: قبض‌های فضاهای مشترک کم شد «و در نتیجه ساکنان کمتر پول می‌دهند»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]},{"n":40,"kind":"match","prompt":"A city cannot meet all its electricity needs from its own roofs.","correct":4,"evidence":"will never produce all the electricity it uses from its own roofs","why":{"en":"Mensah: \"A city like this will never produce all the electricity it uses from its own roofs.\" E is used twice.","tr":"Mensah: \"Böyle bir şehir kullandığı tüm elektriği asla kendi çatılarından üretemez.\" E iki kez kullanılıyor.","fa":"منسا: «شهری مثل این هیچ‌وقت همه‌ی برقی را که مصرف می‌کند از بام‌های خودش تولید نمی‌کند». E دو بار به کار می‌رود."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]}]}],"id":"c-x07-r3-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-07","unit":"x07-r3"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"There is a shortage of installers.\" A shortage is...","options":["having too many","not having enough of something","a short course"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Shortage = not enough.","tr":"Shortage = yeterince olmaması.","fa":"shortage یعنی کمبود."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A question says \"a problem caused by animals\". Which sentence matches?","options":["\"Foxes dig under the fences.\"","\"The fences are expensive.\"","\"Animals are welcome in the park.\""],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Foxes digging is a problem caused by animals; the third mentions animals but no problem.","tr":"Tilkilerin kazması hayvanların yol açtığı bir sorun; üçüncüsü hayvanlardan söz ediyor ama sorundan değil.","fa":"کندن روباه‌ها مشکلی است که جانورها ایجاد می‌کنند؛ سومی از جانور حرف می‌زند، اما نه از مشکل."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Nine paragraphs and seven questions, with \"NB You may use any letter more than once\". What should you do first?","options":["answer the questions in alphabetical order","read only the first paragraph","label each paragraph with its main topic"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Labels make it quick to find the right paragraph for each question.","tr":"Etiketler her soru için doğru paragrafı hızlıca bulmanı sağlar.","fa":"برچسب‌ها کمک می‌کنند پاراگراف درست هر سؤال را سریع پیدا کنی."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"\"‘People worried the panels would be ugly,’ says the architect, ‘but ours look just like tiles.’\" Who thinks the panels look bad?","options":["the architect","other people","nobody"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The architect reports others’ worry and disagrees with it.","tr":"Mimar başkalarının endişesini aktarıyor ve ona katılmıyor.","fa":"معمار نگرانی دیگران را نقل می‌کند و با آن مخالف است."}}],"id":"c-x07-r3-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-07","unit":"x07-r3"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
